@startuml
title Nortadas - Scheduler Flow: fetch weather -> persist reading

'Formatting
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam backgroundColor #adb5bd
skinparam ArrowFontColor #141414
skinparam ArrowColor #141414
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    ParticipantFontColor #ffffff
    ParticipantBorderColor #364fc7
    ActorBackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    ActorFontColor #ffffff
    LifeLineBorderColor #364fc7
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #dbe4ff
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #4c6ef5
    FontColor #ffffff
    BorderColor #364fc7
}

' Runs hourly (US009). Detection is NOT part of this flow - see the note below.

participant "WeatherDataScheduler\n<<scheduler>>" as Scheduler
participant "FetchWeatherUseCase\n<<application>>" as UseCase
participant "BeachRepositoryPort\n<<port>>" as BeachRepo
participant "WeatherClientPort\n<<port>>" as WClient
participant "OpenMeteoClientAdapter\n<<infrastructure>>" as OpenMeteo
participant "WeatherReadingRepositoryPort\n<<port>>" as ReadingRepo

note over Scheduler
  @Scheduled(cron = nortadas.weather.scheduler.cron),
  default hh:23:37 - deliberately NOT the top of the
  hour: a real hh:00:00 run drew HTTP 503 "service is
  overloaded" from Open-Meteo's free tier (issue #50).
end note

Scheduler -> UseCase : fetchWeatherForAllBeaches()\n-> fetchAllBeaches()
activate UseCase

UseCase -> BeachRepo : findAll()
activate BeachRepo
BeachRepo --> UseCase : List<Beach>
deactivate BeachRepo

loop for each Beach
    UseCase -> WClient : fetchCurrent(beachId, latitude, longitude)
    activate WClient
    WClient -> OpenMeteo : GET /forecast?current=wind_speed_10m,\nwind_direction_10m,temperature_2m,weather_code
    activate OpenMeteo
    OpenMeteo --> WClient : wind + air temperature + WMO weather_code
    deactivate OpenMeteo

    WClient -> OpenMeteo : GET /marine?current=sea_surface_temperature
    activate OpenMeteo
    OpenMeteo --> WClient : sea-surface temperature
    deactivate OpenMeteo

    note right of OpenMeteo
      Two calls per beach: Open-Meteo splits the data across
      the forecast and marine APIs (ADR-004). The adapter
      combines both into one domain WeatherReading, so the
      provider's JSON shape never crosses the port.
      Connect/read timeouts are configured so a slow beach
      cannot hang the sweep (issue #50).
    end note

    WClient --> UseCase : WeatherReading
    deactivate WClient

    UseCase -> ReadingRepo : save(reading)
    activate ReadingRepo
    ReadingRepo --> UseCase : persisted WeatherReading
    deactivate ReadingRepo

    alt fetch or persist fails
        note over UseCase : log error, continue to next beach\n(one failed beach must not crash the sweep - US009)
    end
end

UseCase --> Scheduler : done
deactivate UseCase

note over UseCase, ReadingRepo
  Nortada detection deliberately does NOT run here.
  A reading stores only raw observations; NortadaStatus
  (and WeatherCondition) are derived on demand at READ
  time by the query use cases and never persisted, so
  the rules can change without a data migration
  (see beach-request-flows.puml, ADR-005).
end note

@enduml
